    "abstract": "<p>This chapter explores some of the experiments looking for dark matter in the galaxy. It reviews astronomical observations that have provided conclusive evidence of dark matter's existence, noting how experimenters now face the challenge of measuring its properties. It also mentions axions, which are the main dark matter candidates that result from the strong interaction and heavy particles from extensions to the Standard Model. The chapter discusses what astronomers know about dark matter near the Earth. It describes the way dark matter might weakly interact with normal matter and be detected in an experiment, including several different kinds of dark matter experiments that are currently operating.</p>",
